cartridge "CANADAIR/JEAN-FRANCOIS SEHAN/1984"

' CANADAIR - ColecoVision version of the Oric game by Jean-Francois Sehan
' ("L'Oric a l'affiche", Editions du P.S.I., 1984). Adapted by Amy & Claude,
' Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from this file, ../_common/amy/core.alexis,
' pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME (as in the book): a forest burns, each column of flames has a
' random height that grows with the level. Your water bomber flies across
' the screen by itself; it turns at both edges and comes one row lower at
' each turn on the left. A button drops water: one load in the air at a
' time, falling straight down; a load that lands on a flame puts out three
' cells of it. Touching a flame is a crash. Reaching the bottom row (the
' tree tops) wins the level; the next fire is taller.
'
' CONTROLS: a button drops water. Joystick left/right: push the way the
' plane flies to go faster, push back to slow down. Title: up/down choose,
' left/right change the starting level, a button confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - Play field: columns 2-29, rows 3-20 (the Oric's 33 x 21); flames burn
'   on columns 5-28, columns 2-4 are a lake.
' - Three lives instead of one; a crash costs a life and starts a new fire
'   on the same level (the book went back to level 1).
' - Joystick speed control (new), and a water tank of 6 loads, filled again
'   over the lake at each left turn (new: some care with the water).
' - Putting out every flame wins the level at once, with a bonus for the
'   rows not flown (the book kept the plane sweeping down to the bottom).
' - From level 2 the fire grows back slowly (one cell at a time), never
'   to within three rows of the plane; level 4 on, it can also spread to a
'   put-out column next to a big fire. Tallest starting flame, speed and
'   regrowth come from tables for levels 1-16 (then the last values),
'   tuned with model/canasim.py and checked with tests/bot.mjs.
' - The steam puff of a hit never holds the next load back (one load in
'   the air at a time, as in the book).
' - The plane's speed: 1 pixel a frame for its first three rows (the book's
'   half step), then faster, a little more each level.
' - Colour, animation, music and sound effects are new; the Oric's ZAP,
'   EXPLODE and SHOOT are kept as the cues.

